07-11T17:56:27.943","@type":"sc:Dataset","name":"Social Media Sentiment Analysis: AI Trends 2026","url":"https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/dreamtensor/social-media-sentiment-analysisai-trend-2026/versions/1","description":"# **\uD83E\uDDFEIntroduction:**\n  This dataset is a collection of **2,200 synthetic social media posts** about Artificial Intelligence trends in 2026.Each record include information about platform ,user details, post contents, engagement(like,comment etc), sentiments, emotions, toxicity score, sarcasm detection, spam flag and topic category.This dataset can be used by beginners and researchers to explore data analysis, NLP, Machine learning and data visualization.\n\n# **\uD83D\uDCD1Dataset Overview:**\n- **2,200 records**\n- **27  attributes**\n- **Missing values: Mention(column) contain too many missing values.**\n\n# **\uD83D\uDE2FWhat makes this dataset interesting?**\n\n Social media is much more than text.\n\nA single post can answer many questions:\n\n* Why do some posts receive thousands of likes while others are ignored?\n* Are positive posts shared more often than negative ones?\n* Does sarcasm reduce engagement?\n* Are trending topics generally more positive or more controversial?\n* Can toxicity influence popularity?\n* Are verified users treated differently by the audience?\n* Which AI topics generate the most discussion?\n\nThis dataset makes it possible to investigate all of these questions.\n\n# **\uD83E\uDD16 Machine Learning Opportunities:**\nThis dataset supports a wide range of machine learning projects.\n\n### Classification\n\n* Sentiment Prediction\n* Emotion Classification\n* Spam Detection\n* Sarcasm Detection\n* Trending Topic Prediction\n\n### Regression\n\n* Engagement Score Prediction\n* Like Count Prediction\n* Comment Count Prediction\n* Share Count Prediction\n* Toxicity Score Prediction\n\n### Natural Language Processing\n\n* Text Classification\n* Feature Engineering\n* Word Frequency Analysis\n* Word Embeddings\n\n## **\uD83C\uDF93 Who Can Use This Dataset?**\n\nThis dataset is suitable for:\n\n* Students learning data science.\n* Beginners practicing Python, Pandas, and SQL.\n* Machine learning enthusiasts.\n* NLP researchers.\n* Data analysts creating dashboards.\n* Instructors preparing classroom exercises.\n* Anyone building a portfolio project.\n\nNo matter your experience level, the dataset offers something valuable to explore.\n\n\n# \uD83D\uDE80 Final Thoughts:\n\nThis dataset was created to make learning practical, interactive, and enjoyable. Instead of working with isolated text samples, learners can explore an entire social media ecosystem from user behavior and engagement to sentiment, emotions, toxicity, and AI discussions.\nWhether you\u0027re practicing Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA), building your first machine learning model, creating an NLP pipeline, or designing an interactiv dashboard, this dataset provides a realistic and feature rich environment to strengthen your data science skills.\n  \nHeader file image used from pinterest."}